thub.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected. Code looks good to me.\r\n\r\n**Testing project:** [test_softbody_point_radius.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20377214/test_softbody_point_radius.zip)\r\n\r\nExample at 20 ticks per second:\r\n\r\n### Physics interpolation disabled\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bcbf9c99-ce18-42eb-a6ae-652ef5a9d3e6\r\n\r\n### Physics interpolation enabled\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f58c4b3e-572d-453d-a873-2e8477cbb6e4\r\n\r\n\r\nOf course, SoftBody simulation quality greatly varies depending on the physics tick rate. In practice, you'll want to use 30 tps or more for cloth whenever possible.\r\n\r\nExample at 1 tick per second so you can see it in more detail :slightly_smiling_face: \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b4464086-9bb5-485b-9a61-b3c0f86b7c11\r\n\r\nDuring the first tick, all SoftBodies are positioned at the global world origin. They move to the correct position on the second physics tick. Is there a way we could avoid this?","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106863#pullrequestreview-2882688257","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106863","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106863#pullrequestreview-2882688257"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106863"}},"submitted_at":"2025-05-30T22:12:54Z","commit_id":null},{"id":2890191516,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6sRNKc","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Works great now :slightly_smiling_face: I can confirm the initial interpolation issue is fixed (tested on both physics engines, just in case).","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106863#pullrequestreview-2890191516","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106863","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106863#pullrequestreview-2890191516"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106863"}},"submitted_at":"2025-06-02T23:30:26Z","commit_id":"cc52fd777ea9fcbb6e121154860b4ee14af3724f"},{"id":2895813655,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6smpwX","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?u=2b8b17ce969861380874563b333a546e0bbaab56&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred